{"id":"p1m4","name":"Latest status per order","lang":"pyspark","entry":"solve","params":["spark","events_df"],"limit_s":30,"ordered":false,"desc":"<p><code>events_df</code> stores every status change of every order: <code>order_id</code> (string), <code>status</code> (string) and <code>updated_at</code> (timestamp). Timestamps of one order are all different.</p>\n<p>Return one row per order with its latest status: columns <code>order_id</code>, <code>status</code>, <code>updated_at</code>. Row order does not matter.</p>\n<h4>Example</h4><p><code>events_df</code>:</p><div class=\"tblw\"><table><tr><th>order_id</th><th>status</th><th>updated_at</th></tr><tr><td>O1</td><td>created</td><td>2026-03-01 10:00:00</td></tr><tr><td>O1</td><td>paid</td><td>2026-03-01 10:05:00</td></tr><tr><td>O2</td><td>created</td><td>2026-03-01 11:00:00</td></tr><tr><td>O1</td><td>shipped</td><td>2026-03-02 09:00:00</td></tr></table></div><p>the output should be</p><div class=\"tblw\"><table><tr><th>order_id</th><th>status</th><th>updated_at</th></tr><tr><td>O1</td><td>shipped</td><td>2026-03-02 09:00:00</td></tr><tr><td>O2</td><td>created</td><td>2026-03-01 11:00:00</td></tr></table></div><div class=\"lim\"><b>[execution time limit]</b> 30 seconds (pyspark)<br><b>[memory limit]</b> 2 GB</div>","starter":"from pyspark.sql import SparkSession, DataFrame, functions as F\nfrom pyspark.sql.window import Window\n\n\ndef solve(spark: SparkSession, events_df: DataFrame) -> DataFrame:\n    # write your code here\n    return events_df\n","hints":["Window.partitionBy(\"order_id\").orderBy(F.col(\"updated_at\").desc()) puis F.row_number().over(w).","Garde rn = 1 puis .drop(\"rn\")."],"summary_fr":"Pour chaque commande, garde seulement l'événement le plus récent (updated_at le plus grand). Ordre des lignes libre.","tags":["Window","row_number"],"minutes":5,"source":"Kata Lab","files":null,"visible":[{"input":{"events_df":{"__df__":{"schema":"order_id STRING, status STRING, updated_at TIMESTAMP","rows":[